#4850
stray object~
a stray object~
An object no zone's range claims lies here.~
   #4850 is below every zone's range -- 4900 is the lowest bottom in
this corpus -- so it is read out of zone 50's file and written into
zone 49's, the lowest zone. That is one of fallbackZone's two branches;
#5150 below is the other, and with a single zone they cannot disagree.
   It is first in this file rather than last because the C looks records
up by binary search over one flat table in load order (real_object,
db.c:2828-2846), so vnums have to ascend across every indexed file. A
corpus that broke that would be invalid rather than hostile.
~
